WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:10.567
MasterRecord Steward. Master records from three disagreeing sources - justified changes approved, the rest held for a person, nothing else touched.

00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:22.335
Scene 1. A master workbook with history and reference rows, and three feeds that disagree in planted ways. The registry - it is the authority for that field.

00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:31.573
Scene 2. Every field is resolved. Five changes are justified, four cases are held, one workshop is out of scope. No source gave any certification. Unknown is

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:39.429
not the same as not certified, so a person decides.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:51.524
Scene 3. The registrar approves the changes and settles two holds with a reason. Two stay open. A resolution, an approver role and a rationale.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:01:00.558
Scene 4. A dry run shows exactly which cells would change. No - a dry run only reports.

00:01:01.983 --> 00:01:08.978
Scene 5. Apply: verified backup, decided cells written, a new Changes tab, and proof that 309 other cells are unchanged. It is untouched; the new changes go on

00:01:08.978 --> 00:01:15.973
a new dated tab.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:25.421
Scene 6. The same decisions are applied again. None. Each decision is recognised by its hash.

00:01:26.783 --> 00:01:36.593
Scene 7. The next proposal run shows only the two undecided holds. Their decisions are recorded and the master now holds the decided value.

00:01:37.917 --> 00:01:42.146
The review queue: each hold with the evidence from every source.

00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:49.987
The new Changes tab: old value, new value, decision, role, reason.

00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:58.791
What this run showed: Authority wins; disagreements are held, never guessed. Unknown kept apart from ineligible. Only approved cells changed; history intact.

00:01:58.791 --> 00:02:05.799
Applying twice changes nothing.
